=====================================================================================
PART A - DESIGN FACTS
=====================================================================================
Board / device
  - ZCU208, device xczu48dr (ZU48DR), CLK104 clock module, XM655 balun card
  - Based on Xilinx example "DDS Compiler for DAC and System ILA for ADC Capture" (2020.2),
    rebuilt in a newer Vivado/Vitis (2025.2, Vitis Unified IDE, SDT flow)

Signal path
  DDS Compiler (10 MHz sine) -> AXIS FIFO -> RFDC DAC Tile228 (tile 0) Ch0
      -> XM655 LF balun -> coax -> XM655 LF balun -> RFDC ADC Tile226 (tile 2) Ch0
      -> m20_axis -> System ILA

Converter settings
  - DAC and ADC sample rate      : 1.47456 GSPS, internal tile PLL enabled
  - Tile PLL reference           : 184.32 MHz from LMK04828B on CLK104
                                   (DCLK_OUT6 -> DAC228, DCLK_OUT12 -> ADC226)
  - PLL                          : VCO 8847.36 MHz, FbDiv 48, M 6, R 1
  - DAC: Real output, Interpolation x8, coarse mixer 0, Nyquist zone 1, 20 mA output
  - ADC: Real input, Decimation x8, coarse mixer 0, Nyquist zone 1, AC coupled, Cal Mode2
  - 1 sample per AXI4-Stream beat, AXIS clock = 1.47456 GHz / 8 = 184.32 MHz
  - DAC and ADC AXIS clocks both come from clk_dac0 (DAC tile clock output)

Clocking dependency (most important fact for debug)
  - The LMK04828B on CLK104 is NOT configured at power-up. The bare-metal app
    (RFSOC.elf) programs it through an I2C->SPI bridge, then starts the RFDC tiles.
  - clk_dac0 (184.32 MHz) only exists after the DAC tile PLL locks.
  - The System ILA, DDS and AXIS FIFO are clocked by clk_dac0.
  => Without the app running successfully, there is NO ILA clock and Vivado
     cannot see the ILA. Always: app first, Vivado second.

Other blocks in the block design
  - zynq_ultra_ps_e_0 (PS), AXI interconnect, proc_sys_reset_0
  - axi_gpio_spi_mux (drives clk104_spi_mux_sel - selects LMK/LMX on CLK104 SPI)
  - vio_0 (VIO), util_ds_buf, xlconstant
  - LMX2594 outputs are powered down (only the LMK is used)

Software
  - Standalone (bare-metal) app on psu_cortexa53_0, uses xrfdc driver + libmetal
  - In the 2025.2 SDT flow the app calls XRFdc_LookupConfig() with the base address
    (XPAR_XRFDC_0_BASEADDR) instead of a device ID
  - App prints to PS UART at 115200 8N1

Expected numbers in the ILA
  - 10 MHz at 184.32 MSPS -> 18.432 samples per period -> 5 periods ~ 92 samples
  - slot_0 TDATA = DDS output (large amplitude), slot_1 TDATA = ADC (smaller, same freq)


=====================================================================================
PART B - SETUP: FOLDER, FILES, SCRIPTS
=====================================================================================
Final folder:
  ~/zcu208_dds_ila/
      design_1_wrapper.bit   bitstream                (Vivado impl_1)
      design_1_wrapper.ltx   ILA probes file          (Vivado impl_1, SAME run as .bit)
      fsbl.elf               FSBL                     (Vitis platform)
      RFSOC.elf              application              (Vitis app)
      design_1_wrapper.xsa   hardware export          (only for PART F fallback)
      boot.tcl               xsdb boot script
      ila.tcl                Vivado ILA script

B1. Copy the files (edit the 4 variables first) ------------------------------------

VV=/path/to/vv                  # Vivado project folder (contains vv.xpr)
WS=/path/to/vitis_workspace     # Vitis workspace
PLAT=design_1_wrapper           # Vitis platform component name
APP=RFSOC                       # Vitis application component name

mkdir -p ~/zcu208_dds_ila
cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
cp $VV/vv.runs/impl_1/design_1_wrapper.bit .
cp $VV/vv.runs/impl_1/design_1_wrapper.ltx .
cp $WS/$PLAT/export/$PLAT/sw/boot/fsbl.elf .
cp $WS/$APP/build/$APP.elf ./RFSOC.elf
cp $VV/design_1_wrapper.xsa .  2>/dev/null
ls -l

If any cp fails, find the file and copy it manually:
  find $VV -name "*.bit" -o -name "*.ltx" -o -name "*.xsa"
  find $WS -name "fsbl*.elf" -o -name "$APP.elf"

Sanity checks on the files:
  - .bit and .ltx must have nearly the same timestamp (same implementation run)
  - fsbl.elf and RFSOC.elf must be built from the XSA exported from that same run
      ls -l --time-style=full-iso ~/zcu208_dds_ila

B2. Create boot.tcl ------------------------------------------------------------------

cat > ~/zcu208_dds_ila/boot.tcl <<'EOF'
# boot.tcl - JTAG boot: reset -> program PL -> FSBL -> app
set here [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]]
set bit  $here/design_1_wrapper.bit
set fsbl $here/fsbl.elf
set app  $here/RFSOC.elf
foreach f [list $bit $fsbl $app] {
    if {![file exists $f]} { error "missing file: $f" }
}

connect
puts "---- JTAG targets ----"; puts [targets]

targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*PSU*"}
rst -system
after 3000

puts "Programming PL ..."
fpga -file $bit
puts [fpga -state]

puts "Running FSBL ..."
targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*A53*#0"}
rst -processor -clear-registers
dow $fsbl
set bp [bpadd -addr &XFsbl_Exit]
con -block -timeout 60
bpremove $bp
puts "FSBL finished"

puts "Running application ..."
targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*A53*#0"}
rst -processor
dow $app
con
puts "Done - application is running"
puts [targets]
disconnect
EOF

B3. Create ila.tcl -------------------------------------------------------------------

cat > ~/zcu208_dds_ila/ila.tcl <<'EOF'
# ila.tcl - attach Vivado to the RUNNING design and capture the System ILA
# Never programs the device (that would reset the RF data converter).
set here [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]]
set ltx  $here/design_1_wrapper.ltx

open_hw_manager
connect_hw_server -url localhost:3121
open_hw_target
set dev [get_hw_devices xczu48dr_0]
current_hw_device $dev
set_property PROBES.FILE      $ltx $dev
set_property FULL_PROBES.FILE $ltx $dev
refresh_hw_device $dev

puts "ILAs found: [get_hw_ilas -of_objects $dev]"
puts "VIOs found: [get_hw_vios -of_objects $dev]"

set ila [lindex [get_hw_ilas -of_objects $dev] 0]
if {$ila eq ""} {
    puts "ERROR: no ILA. App not running (no clk_dac0) or wrong .ltx. See PART D7."
    return
}
set_property CONTROL.TRIGGER_POSITION 0 $ila
run_hw_ila -trigger_now $ila
wait_on_hw_ila $ila
display_hw_ila_data [upload_hw_ila_data $ila]
puts "ILA capture done"
EOF

ls -l ~/zcu208_dds_ila


=====================================================================================
PART C - RUN
=====================================================================================
C1. Board (power OFF while changing anything)
  - Coax: DAC Tile228 Ch0 -> ADC Tile226 Ch0 on XM655, LOW-FREQUENCY balun SMAs
    (10 MHz - 1 GHz). NOT the high-frequency balun connectors.
  - CLK104 module seated on the ZCU208
  - XM655 seated on the RFMC connectors
  - Micro-USB (JTAG/UART) cable to the PC
  - SW2 = on, on, on, on  (JTAG boot mode)
  - Power ON. Check power LEDs are green.

C2. Open the serial terminal FIRST (to catch the app log)
  - Vitis IDE: open the serial terminal/monitor, pick the board's port, 115200 8N1
  - The board shows 4 ports (/dev/ttyUSB0..3). The PS UART is usually ttyUSB1;
    if nothing appears in C3, try the others.

C3. Boot over JTAG (Vitis / xsdb) - use ONE of:
  (a) Linux terminal:
        source <XILINX_INSTALL>/Vitis/<version>/settings64.sh
        cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
        xsdb boot.tcl
  (b) Vitis IDE -> XSDB console:
        cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
        source boot.tcl

  Expected xsdb output ends with "Done - application is running".
  Expected UART log:
        Configuring CLK104 LMK and LMX devices
        DCLKout06(DAC_REFCLK):  184320KHz
        DCLKout12(ADC_REFCLK):  184320KHz
        The RFDC controller is initialized.
           DAC Tile0 Power-on Sequence Step: 0x0000000F
           ADC Tile2 Power-on Sequence Step: 0x0000000F
        Data Converter start up is complete!
        ------------- Startup Complete -------------

C4. Vivado ILA
        source <XILINX_INSTALL>/Vivado/<version>/settings64.sh
        cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
        vivado -source ila.tcl &

  !! NEVER click "Program Device" / run program_hw_devices in Vivado.

  Waveform display, for BOTH slot_0 TDATA and slot_1 TDATA:
    Right-click -> Waveform Style -> Analog
    Right-click -> Waveform Style -> Analog Settings -> Row height 100
    Right-click -> Radix -> Signed Decimal
  New capture: ">>" button, or auto re-trigger button, or Tcl:
    run_hw_ila -trigger_now [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]
    wait_on_hw_ila [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]
    display_hw_ila_data [upload_hw_ila_data [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]]

C5. Pass check
  [ ] TVALID = 1 on slot_0 and slot_1, TREADY = 1 on slot_1
  [ ] slot_0: clean sine, large amplitude
  [ ] slot_1: clean sine, SAME frequency, smaller amplitude, not flat-topped
  [ ] ~18.4 samples per period (5 periods ~ 92 samples)
  [ ] Unplug coax -> slot_1 drops to noise, slot_0 unchanged; replug -> sine returns
  [ ] Several captures in a row look the same

  Everything checked = DONE.


=====================================================================================
PART D - DEBUG  (find your symptom, follow the steps in order)
=====================================================================================
General rules
  - Power-cycle the board whenever in doubt, then redo C3 and C4.
  - After any "rst -system" in xsdb, Vivado loses the ILA: rerun C3 fully, then
    in Vivado do "refresh_hw_device [get_hw_devices xczu48dr_0]".
  - Change one thing at a time.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D1. xsdb "connect" fails or "targets" shows nothing / no PSU
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Cause: USB cable, drivers, hw_server, board power, boot mode.
  Check:
    lsusb | grep -i 0403          # FTDI device must appear (board's USB-JTAG/UART)
    ls /dev/ttyUSB*               # 4 ports should appear
  Fix:
    1. Board powered? SW2 = on,on,on,on? Replug USB.
    2. Install cable drivers (once, needs root), then replug USB:
         source <XILINX_INSTALL>/Vivado/<version>/settings64.sh
         cd $XILINX_VIVADO/data/xicom/cable_drivers/lin64/install_script/install_drivers
         sudo ./install_drivers
    3. Kill stale servers and restart:
         pkill hw_server ; pkill -f cs_server
         hw_server &
    4. In xsdb:  connect ; jtag targets
       If the chain is seen but flaky, lower the JTAG clock:
         jtag targets -set 1
         jtag frequency 5000000
  Expected "targets": PS TAP, PMU, PL, PSU with Cortex-A53 #0..#3, Cortex-R5 #0..#1.
  Only "PL" / "arm_dap" missing -> board in wrong boot mode or not fully powered.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D2. "fpga -file" fails
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Messages like "bitstream is not compatible" / "device mismatch":
    -> .bit not built for xczu48dr. Rebuild/recopy the right .bit.
  "PL power off" / "PL not ready":
    -> Power-cycle board, rerun boot.tcl (it does rst -system first).
  Check after programming:
    fpga -state           -> must say "FPGA is configured"
  Board DONE LED should light after programming.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D3. FSBL step times out ("con -block -timeout 60") or "XFsbl_Exit" not found
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "XFsbl_Exit" symbol not found:
    -> fsbl.elf is wrong/stripped. Recopy from the platform:
       find $WS -name "fsbl*.elf"
  Timeout:
    -> FSBL built from a different XSA, or it hit an error. Look at the UART:
       FSBL prints "Xilinx Zynq MP First Stage Boot Loader" and an error code.
    -> Rebuild the platform from the XSA of the SAME run as the .bit.
    -> Or use PART F (psu_init) to bypass the FSBL entirely.
  "Memory write error" / "Cannot access DDR":
    -> PS not initialized. Power-cycle, rerun boot.tcl. If repeated, use PART F.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D4. App downloaded but NOTHING on UART
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. Wrong port: try ttyUSB0..3 (115200 8N1). The FSBL banner should appear during
     boot.tcl on the correct port.
  2. Terminal opened too late: open it, then rerun boot.tcl.
  3. Check the CPU is running and where it is:
       xsdb
       connect
       targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*A53*#0"}
       state          ;# Running / Stopped
       stop
       bt             ;# backtrace: which function it is stuck in
       con
     - Stuck in an exception handler / address 0  -> app crashed. See D5.
     - Stuck in an I2C/SPI clock function           -> see D5 (clock config).
  4. STDOUT not on the PS UART: in the platform BSP check stdin/stdout = psu_uart_0.
     Rebuild platform + app.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D5. App prints, then hangs or errors before "Startup Complete"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Hangs at "Configuring CLK104 LMK and LMX devices":
    -> CLK104 not seated / I2C problem. Power off, reseat CLK104, retry.
  LMK readback shows "-----" or wrong values for DCLKout06 / DCLKout12:
    -> LMK not programmed. Same fix. Expect 184320KHz on both.
  Crash at "RFDC controller" / XRFdc_LookupConfig returns NULL:
    -> Base address in the app does not match the hardware. Check in the platform's
       xparameters.h that XPAR_XRFDC_0_BASEADDR (or similar name) exists and the
       app uses it. Rebuild app.
  "metal init failed" / libmetal errors:
    -> libmetal not enabled in the BSP/platform. Enable it, rebuild platform + app.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D6. Power-on Sequence Step is NOT 0x0000000F
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  RFDC power-on state machine steps (PG269):
     0-2   Device power-up and configuration
     3-5   Power supply adjustment
     6-10  Clock configuration (reference clock present, tile PLL lock)
     11-13 Converter calibration (ADC only)
     14    Waiting for AXI4-Stream reset to deassert
     15    Done (0xF)
  Stuck at 0x6..0xA (clock):
    -> Tile reference clock missing or PLL not locked.
       - Check LMK lines in UART log (D5): DCLKout06 and DCLKout12 = 184320KHz
       - CLK104 seated? Power-cycle and rerun C3.
  Stuck at 0xB..0xD (ADC calibration):
    -> Rare. Power-cycle and retry; check ADC input is not overdriven.
  Stuck at 0xE (AXIS reset):
    -> PL side not out of reset: proc_sys_reset / AXIS clock problem, or the
       bitstream was not loaded (fpga -state). Rerun boot.tcl.
  Only one tile fails:
    -> That tile's reference clock (DCLKout06 for DAC, DCLKout12 for ADC).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D7. Vivado: no ILA appears / "Debug cores not detected" / "ILA clock not running"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Most common cause: app not running -> no clk_dac0 -> no ILA clock.
  1. Confirm UART says "Startup Complete" (C3). If not, fix D4-D6 first.
  2. Confirm PL is programmed (xsdb: fpga -state).
  3. Confirm probes file is set and refresh:
       set dev [get_hw_devices xczu48dr_0]
       get_property PROBES.FILE $dev
       set_property PROBES.FILE      ~/zcu208_dds_ila/design_1_wrapper.ltx $dev
       set_property FULL_PROBES.FILE ~/zcu208_dds_ila/design_1_wrapper.ltx $dev
       refresh_hw_device $dev
       get_hw_ilas -of_objects $dev
  4. Warning "probes in .ltx do not match the design":
       -> .ltx and .bit from different runs. Copy both again from the same impl_1.
  5. If Program Device was clicked: PL was reset. Rerun C3 (boot.tcl) then refresh.
  6. Vivado cannot open target while xsdb holds it: fine normally (shared hw_server).
     If it fails: close xsdb (exit), then open_hw_target in Vivado again.
  7. Debug hub not detected: also a clock issue (same as step 1); if still failing,
     lower JTAG frequency:
       close_hw_target
       set_property PARAM.FREQUENCY 5000000 [get_hw_targets *]
       open_hw_target

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D8. ILA works but TVALID / TREADY are 0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  slot_0 TVALID = 0 (DDS/FIFO side):
    -> DDS/FIFO in reset or not clocked. Rerun C3 and capture again.
  slot_1 TVALID = 0 (ADC side):
    -> ADC tile not running. UART must show ADC Tile2 step 0xF (D6).
  slot_1 TREADY = 0:
    -> Sink not ready; with this design it should be 1. Re-check the BD wasn't
       modified (m20_axis should drive the ILA/sink with TREADY high).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D9. ILA works, slot_0 is a sine, but slot_1 is wrong
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  slot_1 flat (only noise around 0):
    -> No signal reaching ADC: coax on wrong SMA, wrong balun (HF instead of LF),
       loose cable, or DAC tile not at 0xF.
    -> Swap cable, check both ends are DAC228 Ch0 and ADC226 Ch0.
  slot_1 very small:
    -> HF balun used (10 MHz is below its band) or attenuator in line.
  slot_1 flat-topped / clipped:
    -> Overrange. Check no amplifier in the path.
  slot_1 different frequency than slot_0:
    -> Mixer or Nyquist settings changed in the RFDC IP. Must be coarse mixer 0,
       Nyquist zone 1, decimation x8 / interpolation x8.
  slot_1 looks like random jumps / sawtooth:
    -> Display radix not signed. Set Radix -> Signed Decimal.
  slot_1 sine but with periodic glitches:
    -> Check TVALID for gaps; recapture; power-cycle.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D10. slot_0 itself is wrong
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Not a sine / jumps everywhere:
    -> Radix not Signed Decimal (most common). Fix display first.
  Wrong frequency (not ~18.4 samples/period):
    -> DDS Compiler output frequency or system clock setting changed
       (must be System Clock 184.32 MHz, output 10 MHz).
  Constant value:
    -> DDS not clocked/not running. Rerun C3.


